{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred","id":874008,"title":"Does Radiation Hurt Kindred ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-25T14:07:14-07:00","id":874008,"title":"Does Radiation Hurt Kindred ?","content":"As the title asks does radiation hurt kindred and if so how much ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:13:41-07:00","id":874012,"title":"","content":"No. They can carry it around and be radioactive to others but it doesn't damage them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T14:37:05-07:00","id":874035,"title":"","content":"Yes. There were some rules in Promethean back in 1e for it. I forget which of the splat books had the rules, but they absolutely were susceptable to it in 1e. Though, it should be noted that it was still less damage than humans took, and it was only in the event of major radiation exposure that would normally kill a person. Radiation from a sunlamp or tanning bed would not have an effect in either edition.<br /> <br /> In 2e, we don't have rules for radiation damage, but I imagine it can take a couple forms. As a Poisoned Tilt/Condition, or an Extreme Environment. Vampires have no natural immunity to either of these things, at least not in the core book. There's nothing in the rules to suggest that vampires will do more than downgrade the damage from lethal to bashing, though it should be noted that many STs make the call that many poisons or extreme environments don't affect vampires. The rules are kind of light on the issue. Its entirely in the hands of the ST, though I imagine Promethean will bring up the issue of radiation again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-25-2016, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T15:01:00-07:00","id":874047,"title":"","content":"Mirrors, p162, 'Vampires, being dead, don't suffer from radiation sickness like humans do. They can still be radioactive, and can actively spread it through their presence.'<br /> <br /> Armory, p123, 'Vampires and other forms of undead suffer no damage and experience no ill effects from radiation exposure. Drinking the blood of someone who has been exposed, however, can cause dizzying effects. Vampires who ingest such blood suffer a \u20133 penalty for the subsequent 12 hours. At the end of that period, the vampire will vomit up three Vitae.'<br /> <br /> Saturnine Nights, p74, 'When it comes to the effects of Nuclear Wastelands and Irradiation Transmutations, science doesn\u2019t so much get simplified as kicked right out of the back door. Zombies, deadly cockroaches and giant bugs populate the Wastelands of Nuclear Prometheans, and behave in ways outside the expectations of rational minds.'<br /> <br /> While Promethean does offer ways for radiation to damage vampires, it's a special rule for Promethean radiation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T15:20:56-07:00","id":874057,"title":"","content":"Cell death and mutations aren't so scary when your cells have no need to divide.<br /> I could see the HEAT from extreme radiation becoming a problem, but that's a different story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T17:57:53-07:00","id":874138,"title":"","content":"Answering the question is far more complicated than it sounds because, &quot;radiation,&quot; isn't just one thing that harms living organisms in one way. Sunlight is, after all, a form of radiation that most definitely harms vampires. So is the heat of a flame.<br /> <br /> That said:<br /> <br /> 2e doesn't have any special rules for this. However there are applicable rules. First is the Extreme Environment rules (which are not listed as inapplicable to vampires) and the Immortality, Injury, and Mortality rules. These combine to a simple RAW interpretation:<br /> <br /> Vampires take bashing damage from 3+ rated Extreme Environments (which includes conditions that could lead to radiation poisoning) instead of lethal with the same rules governing the intervals of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T22:10:17-07:00","id":874267,"title":"","content":"There are two basic types of radiation: Particle and Electromagnetic(EM).<br /> Particle radiation comes from the breakdown of certain elements on an atomic level, while EM is essentially light of varying wavelengths.<br /> I would say Particle has little effect on Undead creatures, but EM can hurt, depending on wavelength:<br /> <br /> \u200bInfrared/heat= Burns if it's hot enough<br /> Ultraviolet/UV= No effect, unless you want to say an ultra concentrated beam acts like sunlight.<br /> Microwave= Boils liquids, including blood, so probably hurts, may destroy/deplete Vitae.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that my sig refers to a Mage using forces to concentrate all the sunlight in a one meter radius into a inch beam.<br /> <br /> \u200bWait, where did my sig go?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 04-26-2016, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T05:06:08-07:00","id":874416,"title":"","content":"When radiation is mentioned most people default to thinking about the type caused by atomic decay, but yeah, I would expect EM radiation to affect a dead body the same as it would a living one.<br /> <br /> It would be unsettling if the chicken had to still be alive for my kitchen microwave to cook it O_o","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:21:15-07:00","id":874603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874047#post874047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mirrors, p162, 'Vampires, being dead, don't suffer from radiation sickness like humans do. They can still be radioactive, and can actively spread it through their presence.'<br /> <br /> Armory, p123, 'Vampires and other forms of undead suffer no damage and experience no ill effects from radiation exposure. Drinking the blood of someone who has been exposed, however, can cause dizzying effects. Vampires who ingest such blood suffer a \u20133 penalty for the subsequent 12 hours. At the end of that period, the vampire will vomit up three Vitae.'<br /> <br /> Saturnine Nights, p74, 'When it comes to the effects of Nuclear Wastelands and Irradiation Transmutations, science doesn\u2019t so much get simplified as kicked right out of the back door. Zombies, deadly cockroaches and giant bugs populate the Wastelands of Nuclear Prometheans, and behave in ways outside the expectations of rational minds.'<br /> <br /> While Promethean does offer ways for radiation to damage vampires, it's a special rule for Promethean radiation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This seems like a legit answer.<br /> <br /> Second: I thought the Sun was more of a mystical thing affecting vampires not that they suffered from radiation damage more than humans do. Because even in an underground bunker, the sun still pulls you to death for the day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Are vampires Immune to poison? Like snake bites? Arsenic? Poisonous Gases?<br /> <br /> <br /> Added: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874138#post874138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Answering the question is far more complicated than it sounds because, &quot;radiation,&quot; isn't just one thing that harms living organisms in one way. Sunlight is, after all, a form of radiation that most definitely harms vampires. So is the heat of a flame.<br /> <br /> That said:<br /> <br /> 2e doesn't have any special rules for this. However there are applicable rules. First is the Extreme Environment rules (which are not listed as inapplicable to vampires) and the Immortality, Injury, and Mortality rules. These combine to a simple RAW interpretation:<br /> <br /> Vampires take bashing damage from 3+ rated Extreme Environments (which includes conditions that could lead to radiation poisoning) instead of lethal with the same rules governing the intervals of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div> Examples of extreme environments: <br /> <br /> <br /> 2 Light snow, heavy storms; too cold to sleep safely;<br /> air pressure causes shortness of breath; sweltering<br /> sun can cause first-degree burns<br /> <br /> 3 Heavy snow; cold causes physical pain and potential<br /> hypothermia; sun quickly causes first degree burns,<br /> can cause second degree burns with time; minor<br /> radiation poisoning<br /> <br /> 4 Desert exposure; heat rapidly causing seconddegree<br /> burns; moderate radiation exposure<br /> <br /> 5 Desert sandstorm, severe hurricane, tornado, tsunami<br /> <br /> It says the &quot;human body&quot; is not equipped for these things.<br /> <br /> I would not equate a human body to a vampire body. Otherwise bullets and knives would still do Lethal not bashing. I dont see how hypothermia would bother a vampire as they run at Room temperature as it is... which is usually about 68... ( that would kill a human ) And the sun comments contradict what was written for what happens to a vampire in the sun. I am almost positive this list was written for Humans.. ( such as ghouls )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-26-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:10:05-07:00","id":874636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874603#post874603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are vampires Immune to poison? Like snake bites? Arsenic? Poisonous Gases?</div> </div> </div> </div>It stands to reason. Though there's a special exception for certain snake venoms in first edition. I'm pointing out it's first edition in case you didn't see it in the quote. Second edition's change to the composition of Vitae may negate the rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire the Requiem, first edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most venoms and toxic chemicals do not harm the Kindred at all. Many snake venoms form a notable exception. Snake venoms often dissolve blood cells and body tissues. They not only inflict points of damage, they destroy Vitae, usually one Vitae per point of damage. Cobra venom also causes heart spasms. Storytellers can treat snake venom as inflicting lethal damage within several minutes of a bite. The amount of damage depends on the snake, but many cobras and African vipers routinely kill mortals with a single bite. Their blood-destroying venom should not inflict quite as much damage to Kindred (mortals are more fragile, what with their need for a metabolism), but enough to make a snakebite a bad experience. Kindred, like kine, seldom encounter deadly serpents in modern cities, but it might happen under various unusual circumstances. A tyrannical Prince might keep a terrarium of vipers for their sheer intimidation value.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-26-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T11:02:21-07:00","id":874695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874603#post874603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are vampires Immune to poison? Like snake bites? Arsenic? Poisonous Gases?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the poison. Snakebites(And other forms of animal venom) fall into two categories:<br /> \u200b<br /> Hemotoxins destroy blood cells, and necrotize flesh.<br /> Neurotoxins damage nerve cells, causing paralysis.<br /> <br /> I would say Hemotoxins should hurt vampires, and destroy Vitae, but neurotoxins should only be a problem if they are supernatural in some way.(Werespider/werecobra, certain Beast Atavisms, maybe some Changeling Contracts.)<br /> <br /> Arsenic and other Heavy Metal(Referring to the Atomic Weight of the element, not the music genre.) poisons would do very little if anything to a vampire's undead flesh.<br /> <br /> Poison gases are extremely varied, it would depend on how exactly that specific gas is poisonous. Asphyxiates mortals, by harming their lungs or paralyzing the muscles? Vampires don't have to breath, so at most this would temporarily make speaking difficult. Blisters/dissolves tissues it comes into contact with, like some form of acid mist? Melts dead flesh as easily as living flesh. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T11:10:36-07:00","id":874703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874603#post874603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says the &quot;human body&quot; is not equipped for these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I referenced the second half of the equation here. Vampires, at least in 2e, downgrade lethal damage (and non-supernatural non-rollover aggravated damage) as the mechanical expression of the differences in physiology. This was down, as far as I can tell, precisely because 1e got incredibly convoluted with this sort of stuff. This kind of weapons gets reduced to bashing, but this kind doesn't, this extreme environment doesn't really matter, but this does in a different way, this toxin doesn't, but this does, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> It seems like 2e just opted to make it all easier and say that vampire bodies take damage like human bodies, but it is far less severe to their undead state which is why anything that's normally lethal to vampires is reduced to bashing. A vampire takes bashing damage from a shotgun eviscerating them at point blank range, and bashing damage from walking around in a nuclear reactor without protection; things that would easily kill a human are painful but easy to heal for vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont see how hypothermia would bother a vampire as they run at Room temperature as it is... which is usually about 68... ( that would kill a human ) And the sun comments contradict what was written for what happens to a vampire in the sun. I am almost positive this list was written for Humans.. ( such as ghouls ) </div> </div> </div>Level 3's cold example is severe enough cold that it can cause hypothermia. Which is severe enough cold to cause other forms of damage in a vampire as their undead body starts to freeze and vitae would need to be spent to undo such damage.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is a general rule. Just like the rules for guns are. The previous sections in the book (again, a thing I referenced) are what dictate if/when vampires are provided exceptions to the normal rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874636#post874636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though there's a special exception for certain snake venoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there are reason you keep going back to 1e material?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T11:20:38-07:00","id":874717,"title":"","content":"<i>Originally posted by <b>Vampire the Requiem, first edition</b></i><br /> <i>Most venoms and toxic chemicals do not harm the Kindred at all. Many snake venoms form a notable exception. Snake venoms often dissolve blood cells and body tissues. They not only inflict points of damage, they destroy Vitae, usually one Vitae per point of damage. Cobra venom also causes heart spasms. Storytellers can treat snake venom as inflicting lethal damage within several minutes of a bite. The amount of damage depends on the snake, but many cobras and African vipers routinely kill mortals with a single bite. Their blood-destroying venom should not inflict quite as much damage to Kindred (mortals are more fragile, what with their need for a metabolism), but enough to make a snakebite a bad experience. Kindred, like kine, seldom encounter deadly serpents in modern cities, but it might happen under various unusual circumstances. A tyrannical Prince might keep a terrarium of vipers for their sheer intimidation value.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> There are 2 examples of RAW from 1E that state that radiation does not effect a vampire. It seems that snake venom is the an exception to the rule that vampires are immune to poison. So my point was that even though there are not examples for 2nd E, I personally would go with what was written for 1st. It wouldnt be too far fetched thematically or from RAI.<br /> <br /> Also I would not equate acid to poison as they are not quite the same thing, they are defined quite differently. Acid effects non living things as well as living, where poison is intended for Living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T11:24:48-07:00","id":874722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874703#post874703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there are reason you keep going back to 1e material?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the rules for vampires in second edition are in one book. When someone asks for rules that aren't in the book, unless the writers answer them, previously written material is often a good indicator of what these rules might be like in second edition. For instance, while I would say poison doesn't affects vampires at all, as first edition noted, there are poisons that explicitly destroy blood and that might have an affect on them.<br /> <br /> Some people say that the first edition rules are still in effect except where second edition rules override them. Others say first edition rules don't matter at all and second edition rules are all that matter. Some people use the rules that just back up their argument. While I could start a dialogue with Basic, asking for their opinions on the matter, it's easier to just post the first edition rules and let them use their own judgment. Plus there's always the possibility that they are playing first edition.<br /> <br /> Do you have a problem with me posting some first edition rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:23:43-07:00","id":874826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874717#post874717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my point was that even though there are not examples for 2nd E, I personally would go with what was written for 1st. It wouldnt be too far fetched thematically or from RAI.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e changed the default assumptions about vampire physiology a bit, so it taking something that was clearly left out of 2e from 1e does seem to be pushing the &quot;far fetched&quot; line a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I would not equate acid to poison as they are not quite the same thing, they are defined quite differently. Acid effects non living things as well as living, where poison is intended for Living. </div> </div> </div>You can't actually categorically make these distinctions, plenty of substances are dangerous or living and non-living things; especially in a narrowing comparison of living vs non-living organic matter. There are plenty of &quot;poisons&quot; that would damage the physical structure of a corpse.<br /> <br /> The difference between a poison and a toxin is not what it does (or what it affects are) but how it is made. Poisons are manufactured artificially, while toxins (which includes venom) are found naturally occurring in organisms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874722#post874722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When someone asks for rules that aren't in the book, unless the writers answer them, previously written material is often a good indicator of what these rules might be like in second edition. For instance, while I would say poison doesn't affects vampires at all, as first edition noted, there are poisons that explicitly destroy blood and that might have an affect on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless material was omitted on purpose because it is no longer applicable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you have a problem with me posting some first edition rules? </div> </div> </div>In general no. In this specific case, I do have a problem with you asserting that the 2e rules don't address the concerns here. You're painting 2e simplifying this stuff significantly as 2e not having any statements on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:38:12-07:00","id":874839,"title":"","content":"Actually the difference here is between venom and other, generic poisons. Venom is only dangerous(toxic) when injected directly into the bloodstream. I've heard (but haven't tried!) that you can drink rattlesnake, or other, venom and be just fine as long as you don't cut yourself and smear it into the wound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:54:12-07:00","id":874849,"title":"","content":"So about snake venom: 2e indicates very clearly that Vitae is not blood, that vampires can lose blood and bleed without sacrificing Vitae. That indicates to me that snake venom would not affect the vampires stores, regardless of 1e rules. Am I missing a more current reference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:18:43-07:00","id":874871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874826#post874826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general no. In this specific case, I do have a problem with you asserting that the 2e rules don't address the concerns here. You're painting 2e simplifying this stuff significantly as 2e not having any statements on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just quoting first edition's rules on it since second edition doesn't have any special rules regarding vampires and snake venom, as you said yourself.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I've edited it to make it more clear. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:31:06-07:00","id":874887,"title":"","content":"In addition to the threat of being a carrier, I would also suspect the development of a new bloodline is plausible if a Kindred became radioactive enough long enough - same way becoming an infectious disease host eventually produced the Morbus unintentionally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:49:37-07:00","id":874906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874722#post874722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All the rules for vampires in second edition are in one book. When someone asks for rules that aren't in the book, unless the writers answer them, previously written material is often a good indicator of what these rules might be like in second edition. For instance, while I would say poison doesn't affects vampires at all, as first edition noted, there are poisons that explicitly destroy blood and that might have an affect on them.<br /> <br /> Some people say that the first edition rules are still in effect except where second edition rules override them. Others say first edition rules don't matter at all and second edition rules are all that matter. Some people use the rules that just back up their argument. While I could start a dialogue with Basic, asking for their opinions on the matter, it's easier to just post the first edition rules and let them use their own judgment. Plus there's always the possibility that they are playing first edition.<br /> <br /> Do you have a problem with me posting some first edition rules?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No at all. Because I can't find radiation rules for second ed so if first can help clear it up I'm all for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:51:35-07:00","id":874909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874849#post874849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So about snake venom: 2e indicates very clearly that Vitae is not blood, that vampires can lose blood and bleed without sacrificing Vitae. That indicates to me that snake venom would not affect the vampires stores, regardless of 1e rules. Am I missing a more current reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it says this in the corebook somewhere that vitae is to blood as pigment is to paint. If you break down the base of the paint though(think: old or dried up in the bucket), it does still become unusable.<br /> Alternately, the part about losing blood but no vitae speaks specifically about blood leaving the body. Perhaps there is a difference if it is broken down while still inside?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 04-26-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:50:48-07:00","id":874960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR 2e FAQ</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">What happens if a vampire feeds on an intoxicated mortal?</span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The vampire suffers the effects of the drug. The vampire may remove these effects by spending one Vitae, but could conceivably be too intoxicated to concentrate enough to do so.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Poisons not specifically harmful to Kindred follow the same rules as drugs. A Storyteller may choose to make an exception for poisons which break down cellular structure, but that\u2019s at her own discretion.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Also see Rose's post here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/89345-blood-and-smoke-and-drugs-and-diseases?p=89768#post89768\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...9768#post89768</a><br /> <br /> regarding poison.<br /> <br /> In short, Vampires are only affected by poisons if they feed from a poisoned human. The only exception is Storyteller's decision, not a standard rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T16:33:44-07:00","id":874985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874717#post874717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Originally posted by <b>Vampire the Requiem, first edition</b></i><br /> <br /> Also I would not equate acid to poison as they are not quite the same thing, they are defined quite differently. Acid effects non living things as well as living, where poison is intended for Living.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bSnake venom, and really animal venom in general, is acid-based.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T16:43:52-07:00","id":874992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874826#post874826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't actually categorically make these distinctions, plenty of substances are dangerous or living and non-living things; especially in a narrowing comparison of living vs non-living organic matter. There are plenty of &quot;poisons&quot; that would damage the physical structure of a corpse.<br /> <br /> The difference between a poison and a toxin is not what it does (or what it affects are) but how it is made. Poisons are manufactured artificially, while toxins (which includes venom) are found naturally occurring in organisms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where on earth did you learn about poisons, toxins and acids?!<br /> <br /> Acid - A substance that falls below 7 on the ph scale, may dissolve metal and is typically corrosive. Such as the juice found in oranges, and I wouldn't go equating that with poisons. Nor would I consider Hydrochloric acid eating through something, organic or not, as it poisoning said thing.<br /> <br /> Poison - A general term for a chemical substance, either natural or manufactured, that has an adverse affect on a living organism when ingested or absorbed. <br /> <br /> Toxin - A specific type of poison, such as an endotoxin. It's essentially the thing in a poison that makes it deadly/adverse. Though sometimes toxin refers specifically to something naturally created, many scientists specifically say &quot;biotoxins&quot; when referring to a naturally produced toxin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2101-reverendk","name":"ReverendK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T16:48:49-07:00","id":874996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874826#post874826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You can't actually categorically make these distinctions, plenty of substances are dangerous or living and non-living things; especially in a narrowing comparison of living vs non-living organic matter. There are plenty of &amp;quot;poisons&amp;quot; that would damage the physical structure of a corpse.<br /> <br /> The difference between a poison and a toxin is not what it does (or what it affects are) but how it is made. Poisons are manufactured artificially, while toxins (which includes venom) are found naturally occurring</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I said poison and acid. Thanks ^_^<br /> Definition of poison: a substance that is capable of causing the illness or death of a living organism when introduced or absorbed.<br /> synonyms: toxin, toxicant, venom; archaicbane<br /> &quot;a deadly poison&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Definition of acid: 1<br /> a chemical substance that neutralizes alkalis, dissolves some metals, and turns litmus red; typically, a corrosive or sour-tasting liquid of this kind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:50:13-07:00","id":875154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReverendK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874992#post874992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where on earth did you learn about poisons, toxins and acids?!</div> </div> </div> </div>School, not Google.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Acid - A substance that falls below 7 on the ph scale, may dissolve metal and is typically corrosive. </div> </div> </div>There's actually more than one way of defining acids. B-L acids only apply to aqueous acids. Lewis acids on the other hand do not (and thus can't all be effectively measured on the pH scale since it assumes proton density in water).<br /> <br /> For example, lithium ions are a Lewis acid, and biological active with the possibility of health concerns from overexposure or overdose (for people taking lithium based drugs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Such as the juice found in oranges, and I wouldn't go equating that with poisons. Nor would I consider Hydrochloric acid eating through something, organic or not, as it poisoning said thing. </div> </div> </div>That's an incredibly narrow view of the range of effects acids can have on organic matter. A large number of organic (and esp. Lewis) acids are actually not that dangerous on their own, but the chemicals they form when neutralized is actually what causes adverse effects (that's actually true of a large number of chemicals we consider harmful; the chemical itself doesn't do anything but when we metabolize said chemical one of the intermediary forms is actually what's dangerous).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874996#post874996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said poison and acid.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the point remains that the two are not mutually exclusive categories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:15:46-07:00","id":875181,"title":"","content":"So...Radiation does hurt kindred ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:14:33-07:00","id":875289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875181#post875181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...Radiation does hurt kindred ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There isn't really a clear ruling on it in the books, just go with whatever you think makes for the best story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T01:08:04-07:00","id":875415,"title":"","content":"1e, no.<br /> <br /> 2e, yes but never more than bashing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:01:27-07:00","id":875588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874826#post874826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e changed the default assumptions about vampire physiology a bit, so it taking something that was clearly left out of 2e from 1e does seem to be pushing the &quot;far fetched&quot; line a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Occam's Razor would be a contra-indication that this is the case. A bird in hand is worth two in the bush afterall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874826#post874826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't actually categorically make these distinctions, plenty of substances are dangerous or living and non-living things; especially in a narrowing comparison of living vs non-living organic matter. There are plenty of &quot;poisons&quot; that would damage the physical structure of a corpse.<br /> <br /> The difference between a poison and a toxin is not what it does (or what it affects are) but how it is made. Poisons are manufactured artificially, while toxins (which includes venom) are found naturally occurring in organisms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you're just straight up wrong. Toxins include any chemical substance that in a sufficient quantity can cause damage to a biological creature's biochemical processes. These vary by creature and concentration. For example, chocolate is a deadly toxin for dogs and cats (known to cause acute kidney failure). In sufficient quantities caffeine is a deadly toxin to humans (consuming 2 entire carafes of espresso in the space of a single hour will give you a large enough dose to cause fatal cardiac arrhythmia--its essentially 2000+ grams of caffeine). <br /> <br /> The difference between poisons and toxins is not, as you suggest, how they are made. Toxin is a descriptor for chemicals that can cause poisoning (both acute and over time) and more subtle damage to metabolic, nervous, and/or genetic processes. There are many poisons that occur naturally. Some examples that you haven't thought about -- Lead, Copper, Iron. The skin oils of the Poison Dart Frog. Holly Berries. Nightshade. Toadstools. Etc.<br /> <br /> Venom is different from poison in that the mode of entry into the body is not either a) ingestion through the digestive tract or b) absorption through the skin. Venom must be injected to be effective. Some venoms are also poisons (spitting cobra venom in particular). <br /> <br /> To sum up, all poisons and venoms are toxins but not all toxins are poisons and venoms. Word to the wise, anything in sufficient quantity can be toxic.<br /> <br /> Regarding the whole acidity debate. Many poisons and venoms (especially) are acidic because the biological processes of the creatures that produce them are also acid-based. For instance your blood is quite acidic and a good thing too otherwise your heart wouldn't beat. Your entire nervous system is essentially one big salt-acid battery.<br /> <br /> That being said, the most toxic naturally occurring poisons that are often deadly to humans are alkaloid poisons. These usually occur in fungi and plants.<br /> <br /> Regarding how this all affects vampires, I'd say that the undead are pretty much immune to most poisons because they don't really have metabolic or genetic processes unless they want to. At best, the presence of poison will make it more difficult (or perhaps impossible) to activate the Blush of Life effect. I would say though, as in all things, storytellers have more than enough space to play it as complex or as simple as the needs of their story and troupe dictate.<br /> <br /> Finally, regarding the question in the OP. Like toxins, the harm caused by radiation depends on its concentration. IMO, vampires are probably partially immune to alpha and beta particles (downgrading any damage just like being exposed to acid or what not). Gamma radiation in sufficient concentration (like at the heart of a nuclear blast or inside an operating reactor) is probably going to be as effective as bright sunlight on them. Afterall, it must be some quality that sunlight has that iridescent and florescent lights don't have that serves as the bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:44:29-07:00","id":875626,"title":"","content":"The quality of sunlight that makes it hurt vampires is being produced by the sun (and not bouncing off the moon, because that would make it moonlight)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T08:35:19-07:00","id":875676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875588#post875588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Occam's Razor would be a contra-indication that this is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually no, that's not how Occam's Razor works.<br /> <br /> Since 2e changed a number of things about vampires, and contains both rules for how to represent vampires as being more resilient because of their undead state, and rules for higher level doses of radiation, the solution with the least number of assumptions is to simply use the 2e material as written (including any developer errata or supplements for it, of which none are so far relevant).<br /> <br /> Applying a 1e statement about vampire physiology when there are statements relevant to it in 2e is a solution that requires more assumptions, and thus would be the less likely to be correct solution when applying the Razor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually you're just straight up wrong. </div> </div> </div>Source that isn't looking up the definitions in an online dictionary?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Venom is different from poison in that the mode of entry into the body is not either a) ingestion through the digestive tract or b) absorption through the skin. Venom must be injected to be effective. </div> </div> </div>You realize that this is self-contradictory, right? Venom does not have to be injected to be effective, venom simply has to be delivered in a fashion other than (a) or (b). A simple example is a number of snakes that do not have fangs capable of injecting venom, and bite open a wound to let their target absorb it into the bloodstream that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, regarding the question in the OP. Like toxins, the harm caused by radiation depends on its concentration. IMO, vampires are probably partially immune to alpha and beta particles (downgrading any damage just like being exposed to acid or what not). Gamma radiation in sufficient concentration (like at the heart of a nuclear blast or inside an operating reactor) is probably going to be as effective as bright sunlight on them. Afterall, it must be some quality that sunlight has that iridescent and florescent lights don't have that serves as the bane. </div> </div> </div>As I've been noting, 2e has a system for radiation exposure in the Extreme Environments rules that can be used to judge the severity of the exposure.<br /> <br /> As to the whole gamma radiation vs. sunlight, science doesn't matter. Sunlight is a bane because of magic, not its scientific component waves. Sunlight harms vampires more than other forms of light because vampires are supernatural creatures and their curse says so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T10:25:55-07:00","id":875748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875676#post875676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually no, that's not how Occam's Razor works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? It isn't the simplest explanation is usually the best explanation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875676#post875676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since 2e changed a number of things about vampires, and contains both rules for how to represent vampires as being more resilient because of their undead state, and rules for higher level doses of radiation, the solution with the least number of assumptions is to simply use the 2e material as written (including any developer errata or supplements for it, of which none are so far relevant).<br /> <br /> Applying a 1e statement about vampire physiology when there are statements relevant to it in 2e is a solution that requires more assumptions, and thus would be the less likely to be correct solution when applying the Razor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I have 1e rules in hand. It's less work to make them fit than it is to invent whole cloth. The real question is, knowing that vampires don't have human metabolisms, why assume that things that effect human metabolisms affect inhuman metabolisms? That seems like quite an assumption to make. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875676#post875676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Source that isn't looking up the definitions in an online dictionary?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while it is online, but MedLine Plus, a product of the National Library of Medicine seems pretty authoritative. You should be able to find a paper copy at your local library, assuming they have the budget to purchase redundant paper copies for free things online.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875676#post875676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You realize that this is self-contradictory, right? Venom does not have to be injected to be effective, venom simply has to be delivered in a fashion other than (a) or (b). A simple example is a number of snakes that do not have fangs capable of injecting venom, and bite open a wound to let their target absorb it into the bloodstream that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to missing the part where ~A contradicts B.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875676#post875676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've been noting, 2e has a system for radiation exposure in the Extreme Environments rules that can be used to judge the severity of the exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we could use some errata on this because it doesn't seem likely that extreme environments affect the undead much at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875676#post875676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the whole gamma radiation vs. sunlight, science doesn't matter. Sunlight is a bane because of magic, not its scientific component waves. Sunlight harms vampires more than other forms of light because vampires are supernatural creatures and their curse says so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, the ole &quot;it's in the plot&quot;. The problem is that Vampire's metasetting is within a world very much like our &quot;contemporary&quot; world. Successful urban fantasy grapples with the dilemma of science by grasping the bull by the horns and not handwavium. Note that I actually think that the game as is does this and that you're reading too much into the text. More to the point though, this kind of thing is best left to the needs of the storyteller and their troupe. We should not claim any false expertise in these matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T10:52:55-07:00","id":875759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875748#post875748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? It isn't the simplest explanation is usually the best explanation?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree. I have 1e rules in hand. It's less work to make them fit than it is to invent whole cloth. The real question is, knowing that vampires don't have human metabolisms, why assume that things that effect human metabolisms affect inhuman metabolisms? That seems like quite an assumption to make.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with this too. If the information is there for 1E, why invent a whole new set of rules. We shouldn't say a human is like a vampire. We know they are immune to diseases and poison ( unless you feed from a poisoned person, but then you can just spend a vitae to get rid of it ) 1E materials support that 2E statement. So again It would be a safe assumption to say that they are immune to radiation poisoning.<br /> <br /> ( yes I can see being put in a microwave effecting the vampire, but that is not what we are talking about here. )<br /> <br /> Pg 215 2E<br /> <i>&quot;Vampires do not tire, do not age, do not falter to disease or poison, hunting the night where none but the greatest of predators tread. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875748#post875748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, while it is online, but MedLine Plus, a product of the National Library of Medicine seems pretty authoritative. You should be able to find a paper copy at your local library, assuming they have the budget to purchase redundant paper copies for free things online.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> seems like a valid source.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875748#post875748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we could use some errata on this because it doesn't seem likely that extreme environments affect the undead much at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with that. I dont think that anything but the most extremes of situations should the environment hurt an undead. ( standing around near a forest fire, or -100, or getting peppered with flying objects in a tornado )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-27-2016, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:55:54-07:00","id":876068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875748#post875748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? It isn't the simplest explanation is usually the best explanation?</div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn't. Because the simplest explanation would make, &quot;a wizard did it,&quot; a better explanation than things like science.<br /> <br /> Occam's Razor is rather explicitly not about simplicity. The number of assumptions necessary for the explanation is the key factor. As well it is never about which explanation is &quot;best&quot; but which explanation is most likely to be true; Occam's Razor can easily be shown to generate &quot;best&quot; explanations that are not the correct explanation after thorough investigation because it isn't actually about the best explanation but simply a heuristic to guide which explanations have the most merit and should be investigated first.<br /> <br /> &quot;Zeus struck the tree with a thunderbolt,&quot; is a more simple explanation than the science behind lightning strikes explaining why a tree was struck by lightning. However the Zeus explanation requires far more assumptions (a whole series of metaphysical, and theological ones), where the scientific explanation of lightning strikes only requires the relatively small set of assumptions necessary for the functioning of the scientific method.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's less work to make them fit than it is to invent whole cloth. </div> </div> </div>This is a strawman. There's no need to invent anything whole cloth by us as the players of the game. The only people that had to invent anything were the authors of 2e when the developers decided to change things about the game; and that work as already been done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The real question is, knowing that vampires don't have human metabolisms, why assume that things that effect human metabolisms affect inhuman metabolisms? That seems like quite an assumption to make. </div> </div> </div>We don't need to make assumptions. 2e describes the effects of their inhuman state as it relates to things that damage organic matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, while it is online, but MedLine Plus, a product of the National Library of Medicine seems pretty authoritative. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't really consider Medline Plus all that authoritative.<br /> <br /> However some interesting things about that:<br /> <br /> 1) You haven't actually cited anything by referencing a website.<br /> <br /> 2) Medline Plus doesn't have an entry defining poisons; it only addresses poisoning.<br /> <br /> 3) Medline Plus defines toxins as, &quot;substances created by plants and animals that are poisonous to humans.&quot; which means that my statement about toxins being defined by their creation by living organisms is backed up here, not disproven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I seem to missing the part where ~A contradicts B. </div> </div> </div>You said, &quot;Venom must be injected to be effective.&quot; which is both objectively false, and does not abide by the previous sentences definitions of the requirements of venom; the first statement is actually completely unnecessary if the second is true because if all venom requires injection to be effective then ingestion and absorption through the skin are already invalid.<br /> <br /> Of course, you could just say, &quot;Yeah, that was poor wording, venom doesn't need to be injected; injection is just the most common method of delivery,&quot; instead of trying to play formal logic-semantic games over the fact that you said something wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, we could use some errata on this because it doesn't seem likely that extreme environments affect the undead much at all. </div> </div> </div>Citation for anything that says vampires are immune to Extreme Environments? Vitalis managed to actually cite the reference about diseases and poisons (which Rose has since clarified further). There's no such statement about Extreme Environments.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Extreme Environment rules as they are make vampires extremely resilient to them compared to humans without porting in the 1e assumptions. Vampires can easily have more to worry about when the sun rises than taking enough damage from Extreme Environments to put them in significant risk to their long term survival.<br /> <br /> A level 3 Extreme Environment will kill a Stamina 2 human in 9 hours (and a few minutes technically). A vampire with Stamina 2, can withstand the same conditions for 10 hours and spend 4 vitae to walk away completely healthy. Even if they for some reason don't heal anything, they'd last almost a full day before final Death (though they're fall into torpor and would be forced to spend vitae to heal in that state allowing even longer survival).<br /> <br /> So again, we have rules, that when applied mean vampires can withstand far more damage than humans can. There's no reason to change them because for some reason their inhuman state isn't being represented; when it clearly is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, yes, the ole &quot;it's in the plot&quot;. The problem is that Vampire's metasetting is within a world very much like our &quot;contemporary&quot; world. Successful urban fantasy grapples with the dilemma of science by grasping the bull by the horns and not handwavium. Note that I actually think that the game as is does this and that you're reading too much into the text. More to the point though, this kind of thing is best left to the needs of the storyteller and their troupe. We should not claim any false expertise in these matters. </div> </div> </div>Vampire (and the CofD as a whole) aren't urban fantasy first, they're horror first.<br /> <br /> As well, plenty of successful urban fantasy stories don't &quot;grasp the bull by the horns,&quot; and hand-wave plenty about the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'm not claiming &quot;false expertise,&quot; it's the rules of the game. Sunlight in specific is a bane of vampires, not a band of electromagnetic waves created by other sources; as noted moonlight is reflected sunlight as does not harm vampires (it would be a pretty shitty game if vampires couldn't go outside at all).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875759#post875759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So again It would be a safe assumption to say that they are immune to radiation poisoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e and 2e are in alignment on one thing doesn't mean all 1e assumptions are valid in 2e. There's no statement about radiation in 2e the compliments the 1e assumptions about drugs and poisons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ( yes I can see being put in a microwave effecting the vampire, but that is not what we are talking about here. ) </div> </div> </div>Actually, it sort of is. The amount of radiation necessary to kill a human in a few hours is not a small amount of background radiation; let alone enough to kill a human in a few minutes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T07:15:58-07:00","id":876598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it isn't. Because the simplest explanation would make, &quot;a wizard did it,&quot; a better explanation than things like science.<br /> <br /> Occam's Razor is rather explicitly not about simplicity. The number of assumptions necessary for the explanation is the key factor. As well it is never about which explanation is &quot;best&quot; but which explanation is most likely to be true; Occam's Razor can easily be shown to generate &quot;best&quot; explanations that are not the correct explanation after thorough investigation because it isn't actually about the best explanation but simply a heuristic to guide which explanations have the most merit and should be investigated first.<br /> <br /> &quot;Zeus struck the tree with a thunderbolt,&quot; is a more simple explanation than the science behind lightning strikes explaining why a tree was struck by lightning. However the Zeus explanation requires far more assumptions (a whole series of metaphysical, and theological ones), where the scientific explanation of lightning strikes only requires the relatively small set of assumptions necessary for the functioning of the scientific method.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, when you have a world with magic in it then magic being the cause <i><b>is</b></i> a valid assumption. Of course it begs the question of <b><i> how</i></b> the magic worked. This is actually a discussion I've had with my advisor. Occam's Razor can't be used to eliminate things that exist. In the CofD possible worlds magic (and quite possibly Zeus) do exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a strawman. There's no need to invent anything whole cloth by us as the players of the game. The only people that had to invent anything were the authors of 2e when the developers decided to change things about the game; and that work as already been done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually to my knowledge there's still no environmental tilt that adequately represents the effects of gamma radiation (which is an entirely different creature from alpha and beta radiation, both of which I'm willing to concede can be handled as an environmental tilt)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't need to make assumptions. 2e describes the effects of their inhuman state as it relates to things that damage organic matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the list of things that damage organic matter was exhaustive I'd give it to you. But it's not exhaustive (and indeed doesn't need to be). Radiation is an edge case and best left to the individual troupes to implement on their own. No formal ruling necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't really consider Medline Plus all that authoritative.</div> </div> </div> </div>This should have a huge neon sign shouting &quot;Warning Will Robinson! Danger! Danger!&quot; These medical dictionaries are assembled by experts and used to teach the legions of doctors, nurses, and other medical professionals that work all over the world. Yet somehow your expertise is greater than all of theirs combined? Good luck with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However some interesting things about that:<br /> 1) You haven't actually cited anything by referencing a website.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't claim that I was ever citing anything, merely pointing you at a FSMB-approved authoritative source. I note though that your own definitions lack citations and seem to have been produced primarily through the auspices of &quot;seat-of-my-pants-ism&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Medline Plus doesn't have an entry defining poisons; it only addresses poisoning.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wrong! Try again! You're ineptitude at using web resources is no defense.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">For those following along you can find the definition <a href=\"http://c.merriam-webster.com/medlineplus/poison\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Medline Plus defines toxins as, &quot;substances created by plants and animals that are poisonous to humans.&quot; which means that my statement about toxins being defined by their creation by living organisms is backed up here, not disproven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd give you this except that I'm going to pull a page from your playbook and switch word senses. I'm using &quot;toxin&quot; in the colloquial sense to refer to any substance with &quot;toxic effects&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said, &quot;Venom must be injected to be effective.&quot; which is both objectively false, and does not abide by the previous sentences definitions of the requirements of venom; the first statement is actually completely unnecessary if the second is true because if all venom requires injection to be effective then ingestion and absorption through the skin are already invalid.<br /> <br /> Of course, you could just say, &quot;Yeah, that was poor wording, venom doesn't need to be injected; injection is just the most common method of delivery,&quot; instead of trying to play formal logic-semantic games over the fact that you said something wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think you just have poor reading comprehension. Still not seeing where venom doesn't need to be injected. The following phrase seems to be important <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">transmitted to prey or an enemy chiefly by biting or stinging</span></span>&quot; </span>Personally I've never seen a venom that was transmitted any other way. Perhaps you'd be willing to bring forth 10 or 12 examples to show us all how venom is often transmitted by some other means than mechanical injection (i.e., through teeth or stingers)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Citation for anything that says vampires are immune to Extreme Environments? Vitalis managed to actually cite the reference about diseases and poisons (which Rose has since clarified further). There's no such statement about Extreme Environments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, provide a citation that says that they are affected by extreme environments? Or for that matter anything else you say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the Extreme Environment rules as they are make vampires extremely resilient to them compared to humans without porting in the 1e assumptions. Vampires can easily have more to worry about when the sun rises than taking enough damage from Extreme Environments to put them in significant risk to their long term survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean the Immortality, Injury, and Mortality rules, not the Extreme Environment rules. It's getting hard to be sure though. You're tilting at windmills everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A level 3 Extreme Environment will kill a Stamina 2 human in 9 hours (and a few minutes technically). A vampire with Stamina 2, can withstand the same conditions for 10 hours and spend 4 vitae to walk away completely healthy. Even if they for some reason don't heal anything, they'd last almost a full day before final Death (though they're fall into torpor and would be forced to spend vitae to heal in that state allowing even longer survival).<br /> <br /> So again, we have rules, that when applied mean vampires can withstand far more damage than humans can. There's no reason to change them because for some reason their inhuman state isn't being represented; when it clearly is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if one looks at the Storytelling chapter its full of advice on how to change the rules (these options are called Twists) in order to play certain aspects of the game up or down. Just because the old immortality schtick only gets some timey-wimey stuff there doesn't mean a troupe couldn't add some Twist to the old environmental rules to change things up. Like any RPG system a great deal of the fine details are necessarily left for the implementers on the ground to work out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire (and the CofD as a whole) aren't urban fantasy first, they're horror first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I'd say that Vampire is a blend of Gothic, Urban Fantasy, and (personal) Horror. Note the Gothic first and the Horror last.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, plenty of successful urban fantasy stories don't &quot;grasp the bull by the horns,&quot; and hand-wave plenty about the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but Vampire isn't a <i>story</i>, it's a <i>storytelling game. </i>If one is going to successfully run a game then one needs answers for characters who are curious about how things work. And since the Vampire metasetting is a world very much like our own, there's no reason to assume that there aren't scientists and philosophers asking the same questions we ask in our own world. There's no reason Vampires are not scientists and philosphers themselves (and are asking these question--&quot;what is it about sunlight that makes it the bane of my existence?&quot;). And in fact, through covenants like the Ordo Dracul, we know that they are scientists and philosophers and they do ask these questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, I'm not claiming &quot;false expertise,&quot; it's the rules of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? How did you define poison again? Something made artificially? I've noticed that you never argued against my counter examples. Of course, that's because you were wrong. While poisons can be made artificially, there are plenty that occur naturally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunlight in specific is a bane of vampires, not a band of electromagnetic waves created by other sources; as noted moonlight is reflected sunlight as does not harm vampires (it would be a pretty shitty game if vampires couldn't go outside at all).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that's the way it written. I agree that's the way it works. But that begs the question of what <b><i>sunlight</i></b> is.<br /> <br /> If our argument is that sunlight is &quot;light with the quality 'coming from the sun'&quot; and then propose that our common sense understanding is as follows:<br /> &quot;Light with the quality of 'coming from the sun' harms vampires&quot;<br /> &quot;Light with the quality of 'reflected by the moon' does not harm vampires&quot;<br /> then we inevitable end up with some inconsistent triads and defeat by simple logic occurs.<br /> <br /> Consider the following triads the represent the assumptions of the above two statements:<br /> A: &quot;Light that has the quality 'coming from the sun' harms vampires&quot;<br /> B: &quot;Light that has the quality 'being reflected by the moon' does not harm vampires&quot;<br /> therefore, C: &quot;Light that has the quality 'coming from the sun' is not the same as light that has the quality 'reflected by the moon'&quot;<br /> <br /> D: &quot;Some light that has the quality 'coming from the sun' strikes a mirror&quot;<br /> E: &quot;That light loses the quality 'coming from the sun' and gains the quality 'being reflected by the mirror'&quot;<br /> F: &quot;Light that has the quality 'being reflected by the mirror' harms vampires&quot;<br /> <br /> This second triad is what we call an inconsistent triad. The light that is harming the vampire doesn't have the quality of &quot;coming from the sun&quot; but our common sense tells us that it will still harm vampires. Ergo, the quality of 'coming from the sun' is not a sufficient common sense explanation for why the light harms vampires.<br /> <br /> There are a few ways out of this. You could reject D but that makes the whole thing moot so I wouldn't. You could reject E and claim that the light can have both the qualities of 'coming from the sun' and 'reflected by the mirror' but, if we do this then we're locked into either rejecting C or constructing a pair of infinite lists of things that have reflection qualities similar to the moon and things that have reflection qualities similar to the mirror. This can be broken again by doubling down and having &quot;light with the quality 'reflected by the moon' lose that quality and gain the quality of 'reflected by the mirror' which can be escaped from by rejecting C. However, if at anytime we reject C then we must also reject either A or B. Since A is our primary assumption that we all agree that it's necessarily true and it matches our common sense then we'd have to reject B and suddenly we find ourselves with your &quot;shitty game&quot;.<br /> <br /> But moreover, my Ordo Dracul Mekhet philosopher is forever unable to make any progress on answering her &quot;what is sunlight anyway?&quot; question.<br /> <br /> In the main, radiation and vampires is an edge case and it can be handled a number of ways (poison conditions and tilts, extreme environment tilts, twists to existing rules, etc.). The main question should never really be how does X affect vampires but if X affects vampires in way Y, what are the implications for my story? Our goal shouldn't be to crunch out some ivory tower canonical understanding, so as much as it should be to help one another tell engaging stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 04-28-2016, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T07:23:54-07:00","id":876604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=875626#post875626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The quality of sunlight that makes it hurt vampires is being produced by the sun (and not bouncing off the moon, because that would make it moonlight)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What's that? Hesperus == Phosphorus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T08:05:33-07:00","id":876642,"title":"","content":"Well, you see, the thing is: <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/10/0a/6a/100a6a7c2fafbc9e79699fcf584c8e1b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:18:21-07:00","id":876715,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1630_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1630\" data-vbnamecard=\"1630\">Jacob</a> It's pretty obvious that it's intended that vampires work like normal humans except where the game marks differences. The book gives rules for humans, and it notes where vampires differ from humans. For example, where humans take lethal damage, vampires take bashing. It's the only way the game is playable, otherwise you can't make any base assumptions on how vampires work and every single case that isn't explicitly mentioned in the book must be ruled on a case-by-case basis. How are vampires affected by silver? Who knows! The book doesn't say! Obviously it makes them explode on contact. No, it makes sense to assume it affects them like it affects humans unless otherwise stated.<br /> <br /> It also bewilders me whenever people pretend they aren't part of the human cultural zeitgeist and don't comprehend symbolism common to most/all of humanity. The bane of sunlight is the bane of knowledge. It plays off the fact that vampires hide in the darkness, that they can't let themselves be known. It also plays off the fact that humanity is diurnal, and as such the rising of the sun wipes away the darkness and reveals the world for what it is because the night isn't our world.. If vampires bring themselves out into the light, metaphorically or literally, they burn. It works because it's a metaphysical symbol, not because of science or logic. Moonlight is an entirely different set of metaphysical symbols. As long as sunlight is still recognized as its set of metaphysical symbols, it still counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:46:07-07:00","id":876745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876068#post876068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Citation for anything that says vampires are immune to Extreme Environments? Vitalis managed to actually cite the reference about diseases and poisons (which Rose has since clarified further). There's no such statement about Extreme Environments.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Extreme Environment rules as they are make vampires extremely resilient to them compared to humans without porting in the 1e assumptions. Vampires can easily have more to worry about when the sun rises than taking enough damage from Extreme Environments to put them in significant risk to their long term survival.<br /> <br /> A level 3 Extreme Environment will kill a Stamina 2 human in 9 hours (and a few minutes technically). A vampire with Stamina 2, can withstand the same conditions for 10 hours and spend 4 vitae to walk away completely healthy. Even if they for some reason don't heal anything, they'd last almost a full day before final Death (though they're fall into torpor and would be forced to spend vitae to heal in that state allowing even longer survival).<br /> <br /> 1e and 2e are in alignment on one thing doesn't mean all 1e assumptions are valid in 2e. There's no statement about radiation in 2e the compliments the 1e assumptions about drugs and poisons.<br /> <br /> Actually, it sort of is. The amount of radiation necessary to kill a human in a few hours is not a small amount of background radiation; let alone enough to kill a human in a few minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose clarified what happens if a vampire drinks from a poisoned person. You spend a vitae and ignore the effects of the poison completely. Unless somewhere else, She has said that vampires are not immune to poison. Please show me. Otherwise: It says on pg 215 that they are immune to poison and disease and aging.<br /> <br /> so going with page 215... IF they are immune to poison and disease then.. they are immune to radiation &gt;poisoning&lt; . How are we still arguing about this?<br /> <br /> As far as Environmental Extremes effecting the vampire. Let me bring up a few points.<br /> <br /> 3 Heavy snow; cold causes physical pain and potential<br /> hypothermia; sun quickly causes first degree burns,<br /> can cause second degree burns with time; minor<br /> radiation poisoning<br /> <br /> <br /> This statement about the sun contradicts everything we know about vampires.<br /> This statement about radiation poisoning and pg 215 contradict each other as well. You cant be immune to poisoning and take damage from being poisoned. One of them is wrong.<br /> This statement about hypothermia contradicts what we know about vampires too. You get hypothermia when you lose body heat... we know that vampires do not produce any at all. So are they constantly in a level 3 environment or do they need to sit under heat lamps, like snakes?<br /> Heavy snow? it might be uncomfortable and heavy, but it wouldnt crush you like it would a human. You wouldnt suffocate or get crush syndrome as it wouldnt cut off blood flow. You dont have any. Your lungs wouldnt freeze. You might get a bit stiff, but blood isnt what is animating a vampire, so I dont know that they would get frost bite, because they already run at a significantly lower core temp than a human and usually cold is used to preserve corpses, not damage them. <br /> <br /> I still dont see how anything on this level 3 list could kill a vampire or.. even hurt a vampire. But maybe that's just me ?<br /> <br /> However I really do get level 5. Tornado, Tsunami, maybe a sandstorm.. ( though they dont need to breath so there would be no risk of sand getting in your lungs )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-28-2016, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:10:45-07:00","id":876794,"title":"","content":"Vampires should be immune to hypothermia but vulnerable to just flat-out freezing solid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:36:56-07:00","id":876821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876794#post876794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires should be immune to hypothermia but vulnerable to just flat-out freezing solid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. I think freezing solid would maybe be extreme 5 weather, like a trek through Antarctica or some regions of Canada/Alaska. In the same turn. I think they would be just fine when they thawed out (if the sun didnt get to them first )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:55:11-07:00","id":876844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876745#post876745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose clarified what happens if a vampire drinks from a poisoned person. You spend a vitae and ignore the effects of the poison completely. Unless somewhere else, She has said that vampires are not immune to poison. Please show me. Otherwise: It says on pg 215 that they are immune to poison and disease and aging.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so going with page 215... IF they are immune to poison and disease then.. they are immune to radiation &gt;poisoning&lt; . How are we still arguing about this? </div> </div> </div>Because it's a victim of confusing terminology. Radiation poisoning is not the same thing as diseases or chemical poisoning. Vampires would be immune to long term radiation exposure (not that the system models this) - the kind of radiation poisoning that can take months or years to kill a human; because either their nightly reversion would take care of it, or it would follow the clarifications made by Rose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This statement about the sun contradicts everything we know about vampires. </div> </div> </div>See Miana's post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of them is wrong. </div> </div> </div>Rather, poisoning has more than one definition and this is a game not a textbook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This statement about hypothermia contradicts what we know about vampires too. You get hypothermia when you lose body heat... we know that vampires do not produce any at all. So are they constantly in a level 3 environment or do they need to sit under heat lamps, like snakes? </div> </div> </div>This is a fairly poor reading. It says a level 3 cold Extreme Environment is enough to potentially cause hypothermia; not that the damage is from hypothermia. The conditions to cause hypothermia are extremely variable, but for an average healthy human being you're talking being outside in some but insufficient clothing during below freezing weather (either ambient or because of storms/etc.) for this sort of thing to be accurate. We're not talking about a vampire &quot;freezing&quot; to death in 50 F weather, because that's not enough to kill most human beings if they're naked before food and water become issues first (and hot food is more than enough to stave off hypothermia in that situation. We're talking about vampires being in freezing conditions where their bodies are at risk of actually freezing; esp. because they're not producing their own body heat and would be more susceptible to such things. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heavy snow? it might be uncomfortable and heavy, but it wouldnt crush you like it would a human. </div> </div> </div>I don't recall anything saying that a vampire is immune to crush damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You wouldnt suffocate or get crush syndrome as it wouldnt cut off blood flow. </div> </div> </div>Sure, vampires don't get crush syndrome, that's why they'd get bashing instead of lethal damage from such a severe injury. Their bodies would be damaged, but it wouldn't represent any long term threat beyond their bodies forcing them to heal during the daysleep if they don't keep themselves well fed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so I dont know that they would get frost bite, because they already run at a significantly lower core temp than a human and usually cold is used to preserve corpses, not damage them. </div> </div> </div>Um.... there's kind of a huge range of, &quot;cold&quot; here.<br /> <br /> 1) There's no reason vampires wouldn't get frostbite. It probably wouldn't progress the same way it does in humans (but the system is not granular enough to show this besides the vampires taking bashing instead of lethal thing), but frostbite is what happens as human tissue starts to freeze and die from it.<br /> <br /> 2) Cold used for preserving the dead is purposefully not cold enough to cause damage to the body to avoid complications that would entail; you don't want to do an autopsy on a corpse that froze in the morgue. Bodies are chilled for short term preservation, just like storing groceries in the fridge. Eventually they'll go bad because it's not actually cold enough to stop decomposition; just slow it down significantly. If you want to preserve a corpse for longer durations, you need to use chemical embalming or similar fixing methods (and even then you generally store them in climate controlled rooms with slightly colder temperatures, though we're talking ~60 F not &quot;holy crap I'm going to die if I sit in here for a day&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still dont see how anything on this level 3 list could kill a vampire or.. even hurt a vampire. But maybe that's just me ? </div> </div> </div>My impressions of how you're interpreting the examples seems to indicate that you're picturing very different circumstances from what I feel the books are trying to communicate. These are supposed to be &quot;Extreme Environments,&quot; not &quot;mildly uncomfortable environments that overlap with the specifics of the examples.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you're trying to say that vampires are meant to be completely immune to freezing at all, being outside for <i>hours</i> in a blizzard would be harmful to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However I really do get level 5. Tornado, Tsunami, maybe a sandstorm.. ( though they dont need to breath so there would be no risk of sand getting in your lungs ) </div> </div> </div>You know a severe sandstorm can strip the skin off your body, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T12:09:21-07:00","id":876858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876844#post876844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Rather, poisoning has more than one definition and this is a game not a textbook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know you hate this but : poisoning<br /> \u200b <b>Definition</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Poisoning occurs when any substance interferes with normal body functions after it is swallowed, inhaled, injected, orabsorbed. The branch of medicine that deals with the detection and treatment of poisons is known as toxicology.<br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> <b>Acute radiation syndrome</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (</span></span></span><b>ARS</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">), also known as </span></span></span><b>radiation poisoning</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, </span></span></span><b>radiation sickness</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> or </span></span></span><b>radiation toxicity</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, is a collection of health effects which present within 24 hours of exposure to high amounts of </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionizing_radiation\" target=\"_blank\">ionizing radiation</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Radiation Literally POISONS your body. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876844#post876844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is a fairly poor reading. It says a level 3 cold Extreme Environment is enough to potentially cause hypothermia; not that the damage is from hypothermia. The conditions to cause hypothermia are extremely variable, but for an average healthy human being you're talking being outside in some but insufficient clothing during below freezing weather (either ambient or because of storms/etc.) for this sort of thing to be accurate. We're not talking about a vampire &quot;freezing&quot; to death in 50 F weather, because that's not enough to kill most human beings if they're naked before food and water become issues first (and hot food is more than enough to stave off hypothermia in that situation. We're talking about vampires being in freezing conditions where their bodies are at risk of actually freezing; esp. because they're not producing their own body heat and would be more susceptible to such things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't recall anything saying that a vampire is immune to crush damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, vampires don't get crush syndrome, that's why they'd get bashing instead of lethal damage from such a severe injury. Their bodies would be damaged, but it wouldn't represent any long term threat beyond their bodies forcing them to heal during the daysleep if they don't keep themselves well fed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Um.... there's kind of a huge range of, &quot;cold&quot; here.<br /> <br /> 1) There's no reason vampires wouldn't get frostbite. It probably wouldn't progress the same way it does in humans (but the system is not granular enough to show this besides the vampires taking bashing instead of lethal thing), but frostbite is what happens as human tissue starts to freeze and die from it.<br /> <br /> 2) Cold used for preserving the dead is purposefully not cold enough to cause damage to the body to avoid complications that would entail; you don't want to do an autopsy on a corpse that froze in the morgue. Bodies are chilled for short term preservation, just like storing groceries in the fridge. Eventually they'll go bad because it's not actually cold enough to stop decomposition; just slow it down significantly. If you want to preserve a corpse for longer durations, you need to use chemical embalming or similar fixing methods (and even then you generally store them in climate controlled rooms with slightly colder temperatures, though we're talking ~60 F not &quot;holy crap I'm going to die if I sit in here for a day&quot;).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My impressions of how you're interpreting the examples seems to indicate that you're picturing very different circumstances from what I feel the books are trying to communicate. These are supposed to be &quot;Extreme Environments,&quot; not &quot;mildly uncomfortable environments that overlap with the specifics of the examples.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It gets to -50 -60 Where I live. I think that's pretty darn extreme and I also feel that a vampire wouldnt really have an issue because most of us humans do just fine. As for causing Hypothermia. I was basing my thoughts off something like falling into a lake that had been frozen. People where I live take the polar plunge. That's where they cut a hole in a frozen lake and jump in in their swimsuits or naked. While that messes with a human. I dont think it would be too terrible for a vampire. I have had a snow fort collapse on me. It's scary. It's cold and it sucks. While it hurt me quite a bit and scared the snot out of my mom. Considering how resilient vampires are I think they would have been able to dig their way out and be just fine. I think in some of the blizzards where they dump 10 feet of snow on you in one night. I think a vampire could sit under a tree and wait it out. <br /> <br /> I suppose my whole point is that while it is a 3 on the list for a human might be a 1 for a vampire...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876844#post876844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Unless you're trying to say that vampires are meant to be completely immune to freezing at all, being outside for <i>hours</i> in a blizzard would be harmful to them.<br /> <br /> You know a severe sandstorm can strip the skin off your body, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I already said that they could freeze solid.<br /> <br /> I am aware. Bury yourself under the sand. you dont need to breath. Do you still take damage? it is such an easy fix. Wait under the sand until the storm passes. You wouldnt even need to be that far under.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-28-2016, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T14:01:42-07:00","id":876950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876858#post876858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Radiation Literally POISONS your body.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of the things radiation can do to your body.<br /> <br /> <br /> The problem with this whole tangent is the continual assumption that this is the only way radiation harms organic matter.<br /> <br /> Radiation can also vaporize you, but I guess the only thing a vampire needs to worry about in an atomic blast is the pressure wave since radiation doesn't do anything to them, right?<br /> <br /> We're not going to get anywhere while you continue to try pick and choose definitions with zero consistency to suit your points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It gets to -50 -60 Where I live. I think that's pretty darn extreme and I also feel that a vampire wouldnt really have an issue because most of us humans do just fine. </div> </div> </div>Are you regularly outside for hours without heavy clothing on?<br /> <br /> 1) Wearing appropriate survival gear reduces Extreme Environment ratings, there's no reason a vampire wouldn't benefit from trapping the insulating effects of such in severe cold conditions even if they're starting at a lower base-line temperature to the level that matters for the system.<br /> <br /> 2) Time matters. The Extreme Environments rules let you stay outside for a few hours in 3 rated environments with no mechanical lasting impact. If it's -50 outside, do you really spend more than 2-3 hours outside without getting cold enough that you want to get back inside and warm back up (you know heal that 1-2 bashing damage you took since you're wearing appropriate clothing)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was basing my thoughts off something like falling into a lake that had been frozen. People where I live take the polar plunge. That's where they cut a hole in a frozen lake and jump in in their swimsuits or naked. While that messes with a human. I dont think it would be too terrible for a vampire. </div> </div> </div>The Extreme Environments probably isn't the best for falling into a frozen lake (which would be between a 3 and 4 ranking since humans can't handle it for hours, but can last more than a couple seconds). There's a reason why the Extreme Environment rules focus on, well, environments rather than specific circumstances (they don't cover having snow fall on you either). This would fall better under the Tilts system even if VtR 2e excluded them. The Extreme Cold Tilt is pretty forgiving, but models this a lot better as a metric.<br /> <br /> I'd also point out that while the polar plunge is risky... if done right it doesn't do any significant harm to humans, so of course it wouldn't harm vampires. Using either the Extreme Environment or Tilts rules means humans or vampires wouldn't have to worry about damage from a polar plunge done correctly. So it definitely seems to be way too minor compared to what the books are trying to communicate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have had a snow fort collapse on me. It's scary. It's cold and it sucks. While it hurt me quite a bit and scared the snot out of my mom. Considering how resilient vampires are I think they would have been able to dig their way out and be just fine. </div> </div> </div>Except vampires aren't any more resilient against crushing than humans. They downgrade lethal to bashing, and heal quickly. If a human gets punched for 3 bashing damage, and vampire would also take 3 bashing damage. This was true in 1e too. Vampires aren't tanks. Bullets don't bounce off them. Swords don't dent on them. Their flesh (baring Disciplines) is just as fragile as human flesh. They just don't need it functioning like we do. If snow falls on someone hard enough to break a rib, it would break a vampire's rib. Vampires can heal that in seconds though, and aren't at risk of internal bleeding or other complications.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think a vampire could sit under a tree and wait it out. </div> </div> </div>It isn't that I don't agree, I just don't think they can do so automatically for free. It would be a minor cost compared to a human, but it wouldn't be free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I already said that they could freeze solid. </div> </div> </div>Then if it's freezing or below outside they're be in serious trouble... which is within the range of a 3 ranked Extreme Environment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bury yourself under the sand. you dont need to breath. Do you still take damage? it is such an easy fix. Wait under the sand until the storm passes. </div> </div> </div>Yes, removing yourself from the Extreme Environment protects you from it. And vampires have methods of escape humans wouldn't have. That's not really the point though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T16:44:15-07:00","id":877092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=874416#post874416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When radiation is mentioned most people default to thinking about the type caused by atomic decay, but yeah, I would expect EM radiation to affect a dead body the same as it would a living one.<br /> <br /> It would be unsettling if the chicken had to still be alive for my kitchen microwave to cook it O_o</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/n9mlGrn.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T16:58:46-07:00","id":877114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=876950#post876950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except vampires aren't any more resilient against crushing than humans. They downgrade lethal to bashing, and heal quickly. If a human gets punched for 3 bashing damage, and vampire would also take 3 bashing damage. This was true in 1e too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that Bashing damage was reduced by half against vampires. Was that not the case in 1E, and if it was, is that no longer true in 2E? Or have I just been operating on false assumptions all these years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":"Honest question, no snark intended. I'd go and check for myself, but no access to books at the current moment.) 04-28-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:05:33-07:00","id":877119,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that's a Masquerade thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:30:12-07:00","id":877149,"title":"","content":"I do attend a monthly VtM larp, so I'm not surprised that I got that mixed up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T19:29:28-07:00","id":877247,"title":"","content":"I think the argument about extreme cold boils down to effects of body shock, like in Hypothermia which would be irrelevant, and cell destruction via freezing the water inside (which would easily be bruising). Might be best to take it case by case however and apply ST discretion in general, Radiation that causes DNA decay and general sickness is one thing, Radiation that causes burns is another matter entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T20:49:25-07:00","id":877282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/874008-does-radiation-hurt-kindred?p=877114#post877114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that Bashing damage was reduced by half against vampires. Was that not the case in 1E, and if it was, is that no longer true in 2E? Or have I just been operating on false assumptions all these years?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely a VtM thing. In VtM, vampires reduce bashing damage by half, but bashing and lethal cost the same amount to heal.<br /> <br /> In VtR vampires don't halve bashing damage. In VtR 2e vampires downgrade a lot more sources of lethal damage to bashing damage than VtM or VtR 1e (and some agg to lethal). However in VtR vampires heal 2 bashing per blood point spent, and 1 lethal per blood point.<br /> <br /> So part of it is also that VtR kept the idea that vampires are better against bashing damage, but changed where that takes place from how much damage is dealt to how effectively they heal it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:48:13-07:00","id":877889,"title":"","content":"A high exposure from radiation burns and I would go for aggravated damage but you'll have to be close to a radiation blast, otherwise I'd second what everybody else is saying: no big deal for a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:56:07-07:00","id":878189,"title":"","content":"It's not &quot;official,&quot; but I did write up some ideas about this sort of thing that I ran by Rose before I posted here. They make vampires less concerned with radiation (and also, this at the time didn't incorporate Rose's idea about carrying a disease for a week per point of diseased Vitae ingested, but I like that idea). I might revise this just a little bit sometime, but this is probably the baseline I would roll with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/40764-unofficial-rules-option-vampires-and-non-combat-sources-of-harm#post40764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:black\">Kindred resist ailments and harsh conditions that would lay even the strongest mortals low. They are immune to all mundane diseases, though a vampire who drinks from diseased humans may become a carrier for a time\u2014many diseases eventually die out without a living host to propagate them. Likewise, Kindred cannot consume drugs in the same way as the living, though by feeding on someone currently under the influence, a vampire can feel the effects of a drug, too. Indeed, this is the only way vampires may continue to enjoy some of the vices they held in life. If such a condition is unwanted or becomes inconvenient, spending a single point of Vitae can 'burn out' the drug from her system. Poisons usually do not affect Kindred, even those with the blush of life active. The blood-destroying venom of some creatures can damage a vampire's Vitae if the blush of life is active and feigning blood flow through a Kindred body. As with drugs, spending 1 Vitae is usually enough to purge the venom, but damage done to tissue and Vitae reserves remains and must be dealt with normally.<br /> <br /> Extreme environments hold less danger to those already dead. Vampires have nothing to fear from hypothermia or heat stroke. Air pressure means at most mild discomfort and maybe a small amount of bashing damage. Radiation poisoning, desert exposure and toxic fumes cannot generally harm the Kindred. While vampires suffer the same effects of heavy snowfall, rain and high winds as mortals do, their powers give them an edge when navigating these hazards. Vampires suffer no ill effects at all from extreme environments up to level 3, and suffer level 4 and 5 environs like mortals do lower level ones (i.e., they take bashing damage equal to the environment's level after a number of hours equal to the character's Stamina).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}